1
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:23,660
The number of people in the world is growing fast – every year there are about 70 million more people.

2
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:40,540
So, we've got two questions that need answers: Have we got enough space on our planet for so many people? And how can we make sure they've all got enough food to live?

3
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:49,440
Many people eat too much meat – steaks, beef burgers, sausages, etc.

4
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:56,260
That's not good for us and we need big farms to produce all that meat.

5
00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:08,600
The farms already use 30% of all the world's land: they create greenhouse gases and use a lot of water and energy.

6
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:13,600
However, we can do something to help.

7
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:23,500
We can eat meat only one or two days a week, for example, and eat more vegetables – that's healthy.

8
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:29,920
We can also eat some different types of meat – creepy-crawlies!

9
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:38,360
That's right, grasshoppers, worms, flies and lots of other insects.

10
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,220
They're the superfood of the future.

11
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,320
They've got a lot of protein.

12
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:53,840
Protein is very important for our health, and it's good for our hair and our skin.

13
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:59,200
Protein keeps our muscles and bones in good condition, too.

14
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:10,980
There are two more reasons why insects are good food options: insect farms don't need so much water and energy.

15
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:15,000
Also, they don't use so much space.

16
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:23,940
For some people in countries in Asia and Latin America, eating insects is not unusual.

17
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:31,420
But for people in Europe and many other countries, it seems very strange.

18
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,840
What about you?

19
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,780
Do you eat any healthy food?

20
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:40,960
How much meat do you eat in a week?

21
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:45,060
Perhaps you think you don't eat insects?

22
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,680
But maybe you're wrong!

23
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:49,460
Why's that?

24
00:02:50,360 --> 00:03:01,020
Because the red food colouring that is in many things that we eat comes from … an insect called the 'cochineal beetle'!

25
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:04,000
Thank you for watching.
